Z||000010||fiero56||06-30-2001||08:29 PM||||I've still got the original window sticker for my Formula. I bought the car from the original owner at 140K miles, and he had kept EVERY receipt, paper, sticker, everything for the car. When I picked it up, he gave me a big shipping box full of reciepts from the day it left the lot. Unfortunately, I haven't been nearly as good about paperwork, so after 140K miles, the paper trail drops off to just a handfull.||||reg||1
Z||000011||JJ-85-2M6||06-30-2001||08:48 PM||||I have the stickers from both Fiero's I have owned.  You can always get a reproduction sticker from Pontiac Historical Services.  It is I believe $18.00 for vehicle information and I can't remember how much for the sticker (30$$?).  They send you technical info for the model year, the order form for your specific car and an 8/10 picture or two of a Fiero!<P>J<P>J||||reg||10
